        <main id="main-content">
            
    <div class="page-header hh-news hh-module" id="post-header">
        <div class="page-header-bg" style="background-image: url('https://midmich.edu/_mid_images/_news/nw-banner-generic.webp');"></div>
        <div class="container">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-md-10">
                                            <div class="post-category">
                                                            <span>Athletics</span>
                                                            <span>Students at Mid</span>
                                                    </div>
                        <h1>Historic Season for Mid Michigan College Athletics</h1>
                        <ul class="post-meta">
                                                                                           <li>Mid Michigan College</li>
                                                        
                            <li>09 March 2026</li>
                        </ul>
                                    </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
 
                     
       <nav aria-label="breadcrumb" class="breadcrumb hh-module hh-news">
  <div class="container">
      <ol class="breadcrumb">
        <li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="https://midmich.edu/index">Home</a></li>
                            <li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="../../index">News</a></li>
                                                                                                                    <li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="../index">2026</a></li>
                                                            <li aria-current="page" class="breadcrumb-item active">Historic Season for Mid Michigan College Athletics</li>
      </ol>
  </div>
</nav>
                     
                                                              
    





 
<div class="section hh-news hh-module">
    <div class="container">
                
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-8">
                <div class="section-row wysiwyg">
                                        <p>Mid Michigan College Athletics is celebrating a milestone year as the Lakers captured conference championships, earned national tournament berths, and set records during an extraordinary winter season. Both the Men&#8217;s and Women&#8217;s Basketball teams secured spots in the NJCAA Division II Basketball Championships, while the Women&#8217;s Bowling team achieved the highest national finish in Mid Michigan College history.</p>
<h3>Women&#8217;s Basketball Heads to Nationals</h3>
<p>The Laker Women&#8217;s Basketball team captured the MCCAA Northern Conference Championship, finishing a perfect 14&#8211;0 in conference play and 27&#8211;4 overall. The Lakers continued their dominant season by winning the NJCAA Great Lakes District B Tournament, defeating St. Clair County Community College 100&#8211;72 in the championship game.</p>
<p>The victory secured the team a berth in the NJCAA Division II Women's Basketball Championship&#8212;their sixth overall and fourth consecutive trip to the tournament.</p>
<p>Several Lakers earned postseason recognition.</p>
<ul style="list-style-type: square;">
<li>Delaney Seaman &#8211; Tournament MVP</li>
<li>Alexus Dunn &amp; Gracie Mellinger &#8211; All-Tournament Team</li>
<li>Tanner Smith &#8211; District Coach of the Year</li>
</ul>
<p>&#8220;These student-athletes have put in an incredible amount of work all season,&#8221; said Head Coach Tanner Smith. &#8220;Their focus, teamwork, and determination have carried them through every challenge. We&#8217;re excited for the opportunity to represent Mid Michigan College on the national stage.&#8221;</p>
<h3>Men&#8217;s Basketball Also Advances to Nationals</h3>
<p>The Laker Men&#8217;s Basketball team matched the women&#8217;s success with a 13&#8211;1 MCCAA Northern Conference record and a 25&#8211;6 overall record, earning the conference championship.</p>
<p>Mid Michigan went on to win the NJCAA Great Lakes District B Tournament, defeating St. Clair County Community College 79&#8211;73 to secure a berth in the NJCAA Division II Men's Basketball Championship. This is the team&#8217;s first-ever trip to the national stage.</p>
<p>Tournament honors included the following.</p>
<ul style="list-style-type: square;">
<li>Zack Parks &#8211; Tournament MVP</li>
<li>Amonti Greene &amp; Vynce Overshown &#8211; All-Tournament Team</li>
<li>Kaleb House &#8211; District Coach of the Year</li>
</ul>
<p>&#8220;Our players have shown resilience and belief in one another all year,&#8221; said Head Coach Kaleb House. &#8220;Winning the conference and district titles is a testament to their commitment and the culture they&#8217;ve built together.&#8221;</p>
<h3>Women&#8217;s Bowling Achieves Historic Finish</h3>
<p>The Women&#8217;s Bowling team delivered one of the strongest seasons in Mid Michigan College history, finishing 4th in the nation&#8212;the highest finish ever for the team. The Lakers also captured the Region XII Championship</p>
<p>Paige Vallad set the stage for the postseason, earning Region XII All-Events Champion and Region XII Singles Champion honors. Vallad, Lilly Massaway, and Mya Jarvis were named to the Region XII All-Region Team, and Head Coach Jason Robinson was named Region XII Coach of the Year.</p>
<p>At the National Tournament, Jarvis finished 5th overall in All-Events. The Lakers also posted impressive doubles performances, with Aspen Davy and Vallad winning the doubles championship, Anyia Sanford and Autumn View finishing second, and Jarvis and Massaway finishing sixth.</p>
<p>The team&#8217;s historic finish was powered by contributions from the entire lineup. Several Lakers also earned postseason recognition, with Davy, Massaway, Vallad, and View named to the MCCAA Eastern Conference All-Conference Team, and Davy, Vallad, and View earning All-Freshman Team honors.</p>
<p>&#8220;This group set a new standard for our program,&#8221; Robinson said. &#8220;Their dedication, competitive spirit, and support for each other helped produce a truly historic season.&#8221;</p>
<h3>Men&#8217;s Bowling Standout Performance</h3>
<p>At Nationals, the Men&#8217;s Bowling team was led by Evan Daly, who finished 1st in All-Events among 137 competitors, earning recognition as the top bowler in the nation. Daly also finished 2nd in singles, followed by Ty Olsen in 9th. A strong performance in the doubles competition from Daly and Olsen netted them a 10th-place finish.</p>
<p>Evan Daly was also named to the Region XII All-Region Team, and received the honor of being named as a NJCAA Region 12 All-American, the first Men&#8217;s Bowling All-American in Mid Michigan College history.</p>
<p>Throughout the season, Daly was joined by teammates Ty Olsen, Mason Hopkins, Mason Temple, and Trey Craige, who delivered strong performances and contributed to the Lakers&#8217; regional and national tournament appearances.</p>
<h3>Softball Coaching Milestone</h3>
<p>Mid Michigan College Softball also celebrated a major milestone this season as Greg Welch, the team&#8217;s Head Coach reached 100 career wins, marking another significant achievement for Laker Athletics.</p>
<p>&#8220;These accomplishments reflect the dedication of our student-athletes, coaches, and the entire Laker community,&#8221; said Danny Smith, Mid Michigan College Athletic Director. &#8220;We&#8217;re proud to see our teams competing and succeeding at the highest levels.&#8221;</p>
<p>Mid Michigan College competes in the Michigan Community College Athletic Association (MCCAA) and the National Junior College Athletic Association (NJCAA).</p>
<p>Mid currently fields teams in men&#8217;s basketball, women&#8217;s basketball, men&#8217;s bowling, women&#8217;s bowling, baseball, softball, men&#8217;s cross country, women&#8217;s cross country, and co-ed clay target shooting.</p>
<p>For more information about Laker Athletics, visit <a href="https://midmichlakers.com/landing/index" rel="noopener" target="_blank">midmichlakers.com</a> or email <a href="mailto:athletics@midmich.edu" rel="noopener" target="_blank">athletics@midmich.edu</a>.</p>
                            </div>
            </div>
